==Finnish==

===Etymology===
An old loan from {{etyl|gem-pro|fi}} {{m|gem-pro|*rūnō||letter, literature, secret}} or from the Indoeuropean root *reuə- "dig"; compare English {{term|rune|lang=en}} and Swedish {{term|runa|lang=sv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈruno̞]|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|ru|no|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Runous|lang=fi}}
{{fi-noun}}

# [[poem]]
# [[poetry]]
# [[rune]] (only in the rare sense of a Finnish poem, or a division of one, especially a division of the Kalevala)

